{
  "id": "14-term-resize-owner",
  "title": "Only the owner sizes the window; IN without a term SUB does not take ownership; TSTATE goes to all",
  "spec": "5.3",
  "description": "Desktop (conn A) subscribed active at 200x50. The phone (conn B) TSIZE is refused (ERR E_NOT_ACTIVE, non-fatal). A watch reply from the phone (IN, no term SUB) is typed through the existing attach but does NOT move ownership, so the next TSIZE is refused too. Then the phone subscribes active: it owns the size, and the TSTATE with the new geometry goes to EVERY subscriber; the desktop adopts 60x30 (letterbox) instead of drawing 60x30 bytes into a 200x50 emulator.",
  "framing": "every frame: u32be len | u8 type | u8 flags | u16be hlen | header JSON | blob; each (conn, dir) stream starts with the 8-byte magic",
